  [x] Record publication and verify completion on this same issue/Project item.

Acceptance criteria:
  GeoJack is an unofficial learning companion, not Georgia Tech advising, a
    registrar integration, an automated tutor or a guaranteed future timetable.
  The new mission starts unconfirmed in the background without changing old
    focus, modes, positions, blockers, dates, records or frozen definitions.
  The selected ten-course route and semester proposal expose source/date limits,
    preparation, syllabus topics, tools, assessment snapshots and practice.
  Course/semester changes require explicit browser actions and standard stale-
    workspace validation; no actual student record is embedded in public source.
  Recorded status/grades remain self-reported. Conditional specialization/free
    credit totals follow the reviewed rules and never imply transcript approval.
  Academic records and browsing grant no learning checkpoint, Atlas credit or
    inferred mastery. Learning evidence uses existing criteria and save guards.
  Optional academic data survives backup and encrypted change/replay/merge,
    while absent historical data remains absent. Invalid explicit input rejects.
  All mission-supporting views recognize the stable identity. Related learning
    is cited transfer, not automatic completion equivalence or hidden prerequisites.
  New tutorial lessons exercise real controls only on isolated practice state;
    all existing lessons remain in order. Dark/light and narrow views stay usable.
  Local technical completion, human acceptance and publication are separate.
    The November19follow-up authorizes coherent commits, normal pushes, a new
    CareerOS deployment and monitoring. Reuse the unchanged main-push Pages
    workflow and verify its exact source, artifact and hosted behavior.
    Enrollment-account access, student-record publication, unrelated cloud
    writes and inferred human acceptance remain outside authorization.

